subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and H := μHE[n] on ℝ^P. Let M₁, M₂ ⊆ ℝ^P be H-null-measurable, and let θ₁, θ₂ : ℝ^P → ℝ with θ_i > 0 on M_i. Let y ∈ ℝ^P and r ∈ ℝ, and suppose θ_i is H-integrable on M_i ∩ B̄_r(y) (i = 1, 2). Put A := M₁ ∩ M₂ and g := 1_A·(θ₂/θ₁). Then for H⌞(A ∩ B_r(y))-almost every x, as s → 0⁺ (quotients in [0, ∞]):
(L) (∫⁻_{M₁∩B̄_s(x)} ofReal(θ₁(z))·‖g(z) − θ₂(x)/θ₁(x)‖ₑ dH) / (∫⁻_{M₁∩B̄_s(x)} ofReal(θ₁) dH) → 0;
(D) (∫⁻_{A∩B̄_s(x)} ofReal(θ₂) dH) / (∫⁻_{M₂∩B̄_s(x)} ofReal(θ₂) dH) → 1.
